## portus.group — un prefijo de rutas sobre una aplicación.
##
## Un `Group` no tiene estado propio ni un despachador aparte: guarda la
## aplicación y el prefijo, y al registrar una ruta le antepone el prefijo. Así
## se agrupan rutas (`/api`, `/admin`) sin `mount` ni copias de la aplicación.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var api as portus.Group is calling portus.new_group with sigil of app, "/api"
## let ok as result of void to portus.PatternError is calling api.get with "/users", users
## ```
##
## ## Memoria
## El `Group` presta la aplicación: no la libera ni la copia.
import std.ward
import portus.application as application_module
import portus.handler as handler_module
import portus.route as route_module

alias Application as application_module.Application
alias Handler as handler_module.Handler

## Un grupo de rutas: la aplicación donde registra y el prefijo que antepone.
rune Group:
    ## Aplicación donde se registran las rutas (prestada).
    _app as ref to Application
    ## Prefijo que se antepone a cada patrón (sin `/` final).
    _prefix as string

## Crea un grupo de rutas bajo `prefix` (`"/api"`, `"/api/v1"`, …).
weave group_with_prefix with app as ref to Application, prefix as string into Group:
    var clean as string is prefix
    if clean == "/":
        set clean is ""
    return with _app is app, _prefix is clean

enchanting Group:
    ## Patrón completo de una ruta del grupo (prefijo + patrón).
    weave ritual full_pattern with group as ref to Group, pattern as string into string:
        if group->_prefix == "":
            return pattern
        if pattern == "" or pattern == "/":
            return group->_prefix
        return "{group->_prefix}{pattern}"

    ## Registra una ruta `GET` bajo el prefijo.
    weave get with pattern as string, handler as Handler into result of void to route_module.PatternError:
        var full as string is calling Group.full_pattern with self, pattern
        return calling application_module.add with self->_app, "GET", full, handler

    ## Registra una ruta `POST` bajo el prefijo.
    weave post with pattern as string, handler as Handler into result of void to route_module.PatternError:
        var full as string is calling Group.full_pattern with self, pattern
        return calling application_module.add with self->_app, "POST", full, handler

    ## Registra una ruta `PUT` bajo el prefijo.
    weave put with pattern as string, handler as Handler into result of void to route_module.PatternError:
        var full as string is calling Group.full_pattern with self, pattern
        return calling application_module.add with self->_app, "PUT", full, handler

    ## Registra una ruta `PATCH` bajo el prefijo.
    weave patch with pattern as string, handler as Handler into result of void to route_module.PatternError:
        var full as string is calling Group.full_pattern with self, pattern
        return calling application_module.add with self->_app, "PATCH", full, handler

    ## Registra una ruta `DELETE` bajo el prefijo.
    weave delete with pattern as string, handler as Handler into result of void to route_module.PatternError:
        var full as string is calling Group.full_pattern with self, pattern
        return calling application_module.add with self->_app, "DELETE", full, handler

    ## Registra una ruta para cualquier método bajo el prefijo.
    weave any with pattern as string, handler as Handler into result of void to route_module.PatternError:
        var full as string is calling Group.full_pattern with self, pattern
        return calling application_module.add with self->_app, "*", full, handler

test "el grupo antepone el prefijo":
    var app as Application is calling application_module.new_application
    var api as Group is calling group_with_prefix with sigil of app, "/api"
    calling ward.assert_eq_string with (calling Group.full_pattern with sigil of api, "/users"), "/api/users"
    calling ward.assert_eq_string with (calling Group.full_pattern with sigil of api, "/"), "/api"
    calling application_module.free_application with sigil of app
